Challenge ke dono results bilkul Special Integral ki tarah saabit hote hain: root \(\times\) 1 likhein, parts lagayein, (i) mein \(x^2 = a^2 - (a^2 - x^2)\) aur (ii) mein \(x^2 = (x^2 - a^2) + a^2\) likhein, aur \(I\) solve karein. (i) mein jaana pehchana integral \(\int \frac{dx}{\sqrt{a^2-x^2}} = \sin^{-1}\frac{x}{a}\) hai.
Teeno formulas kab lagate hain? Jab \(\int \sqrt{\text{quadratic}}\,dx\) ho, to pehle complete the square (poora square banana) karein. Phir dekhein:
square + constant, yani \(\sqrt{u^2 + k^2}\): Special Integral (log ke saath plus);
constant - square, yani \(\sqrt{k^2 - u^2}\): Challenge (i) (\(\sin^{-1}\) wala);
square - constant, yani \(\sqrt{u^2 - k^2}\): Challenge (ii) (log ke saath minus).
Examples 37, 38 aur 39 mein teeno ki ek ek misaal hai.
